  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals and Requests**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual components, like the dark background, vibrant green accent, and clean font, while keeping the athletic theme in mind. The specific color codes are helpful for consistency. I am also focusing on the user\'s specific request for a login screen.\n\n\n**Implementing User Flows**\n\nI\'m now mapping out the user journey: Register button goes to Registration, successful registration leads to Login, and successful login lands on the Landing page. I am looking at the API response to handle OTP and authentication tokens. The login and registration API calls are now well-defined, alongside their data requirements.\n\n\n**Defining API Integration Points**\n\nI\'m now integrating the backend APIs, focusing on the registration and OTP flow, including resending and verification. I\'ve also detailed the forgot password flow, with its OTP generation and password reset, and the logout endpoint. Separating page code components into separate files and folders is now the plan for easy future management and readability. I am also working on Next.js setup.\n\n\n**Structuring Page Routes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on organizing the application\'s routes and user flows. I\'ve set up the `/login` and `/register` pages, and I\'m adding OTP verification and forgot password functionality. Register buttons will redirect users to the registration page, and a successful registration will route them to the login screen. Also, a login button/link will be added to the top navigation/header.\n\n\n**Integrating OTP Verification**\n\nI\'m now integrating the OTP from the API response into the registration flow. I can prefill the OTP and prompt the user to verify it right after registration, which will redirect to the login. I can also handle the `/api/verify_otp` call using the email and OTP data. I\'m considering auto-verification, or showing a verification screen after registration. I\'m planning to use a success toast for confirmation.\n\n\n**Refining Registration and Auth**\n\nI\'m now implementing the post-registration user flow. Upon successful registration, I\'ll display an OTP verification step, prefilling the OTP from the API response with a resend option. After successful OTP verification, I\'ll redirect users to the login screen. On successful login, the user info and token will be stored, and the user will be redirected to the landing page with the user state displayed in the navbar.\n\n\n**Organizing Components and Files**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the project\'s structure. I am setting up the file and folder hierarchy for the Next.js application, including the API client, auth context, and individual page components. I\'ve designed a structure that separates authentication-related components into specific folders, like `auth/login`, `auth/register`, and `auth/forgot-password` with individual files for the forms, graphics, and cards. I\'m focusing on API handling for endpoints.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_131760"
      name: "run_command"
