  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing API Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `/api/register` endpoint, specifically its deterministic behavior. My focus is on the `FormData` it expects: `first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `password`, `password_confirmation`, and `terms`. The response includes an OTP and the email. I want to delve deeper into how the endpoint handles different input combinations and potential edge cases.\n\n\n**Mapping Endpoint Functionality**\n\nI\'m now charting the complete user authentication flow. I\'ve successfully mapped the `/api/verify_otp`, `/api/resend_otp`, and `/api/login` endpoints. I\'m focusing on their form data and responses. The `login` endpoint is particularly interesting, given the inclusion of `remember_me`. I am now looking at the password reset flow.\n\n\n**Exploring Logout and Reset**\n\nI\'m now investigating the logout endpoint\'s mechanics and the password reset flow. I see the `/api/logout` endpoint requires an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header and returns a success message. I\'m also examining how password confirmation is handled during the reset process and the responses. I\'ve noted a 200 status with an empty data array and a success message for password resets.\n\n\n**Defining User Registration Flow**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the user registration process across different devices \342\200\223 mobile, tablet, and desktop. I am defining the navigation flow, and noting that the \"Register\" button in `HeroTopNav.tsx` should redirect to `/register`, and checking for other register buttons to ensure they also lead to `/register`. I\'m going to add a \'LOGIN\' option to the navbar. For logged-in users, I\'m thinking of displaying a profile pill with avatar, username, role badge, and a quick dropdown. After a successful registration, the user should be redirected to the Login page. I also see that the API returns an OTP which should be used for the verification step.\n\n\n**Refining Verification & Login**\n\nI am now focusing on the user experience post-registration and OTP verification. I am making it easy to enter the OTP (pre-filled or manual), and providing a \"Resend OTP\" button. Upon verification, there\'s a success message and redirection to the `/login` page, even if the user goes directly to Login. After successful login, I\'ll save the user and token in `AuthContext` (persisted in `localStorage`), show a welcome notification, and navigate to the landing page.\n\n\n**Structuring Component Files**\n\nI\'m now focusing on organizing the component files. I\'m ensuring each component resides in its own dedicated file and folder. I\'m verifying the directory structure, starting with `src/lib/authApi.ts` for the centralized, typed API service, managing all 8 endpoints, and correctly formatting `FormData` and handling errors. The `AuthContext.tsx` file in `src/context` will manage the authentication state, while common layout components like `AuthLayout.tsx`, `AuthBrandLogo.tsx`, and `AuthInputField.tsx` are being prepped.\n\n\n**Organizing Auth Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on arranging the authentication-related components into a logical and maintainable structure. I\'m placing the `OtpNotificationBadge.tsx` component in `src/components/auth/common`. Within `src/components/auth`, I\'m creating dedicated folders for `login`, `register`, `otp`, and `forgot-password`, each containing their respective form and card components as described.\n\n\n**Verifying Routes & Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new reset password card (`ResetPasswordCard.tsx`) and checking its placement within the `/forgot-password` flow. I\'m also confirming the functionality and correct routing of the login, register, verify OTP, and forgot password pages. I\'m updating the `HeroTopNav.tsx` component to include the login button, and authenticated user dropdown with Logout, and wrapping all app components with the `AuthProvider` within `layout.tsx`. I need to verify that direct API calls from the browser work without needing a proxy.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_178843"
      name: "list_dir"
      arguments_json: "{\"DirectoryPath\":\"/src\", \"toolAction\":\"Listing src directory\", \"toolSummary\":\"List src directory\"}"
