  planner_response {
    response: "Login and Registration pages matching the visual design of the Kratos Fitness landing page have been implemented, along with OTP verification, password recovery, and session management.\n\n### Key Additions & Features\n\n1. **Brand-Matched Design & Layout**\n   - **Visual Identity**: Implemented dark carbon palette (`#0E1012`, `#121417`), high-contrast lime green accents (`#71AC16`), Satoshi typography, organic droplet silhouettes, and athletic imagery matching the landing page.\n   - **Split Screen Presentation**: Desktop view displays an athlete hero showcase alongside the interactive form card; smoothly adapts to a focused card on mobile and tablet.\n\n2. **Registration Flow & OTP Integration (`/register`)**\n   - Form fields: `first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `password`, `password_confirmation`, and `terms` sent via `multipart/form-data` to `/api/register`.\n   - **OTP from API Response**: When the server returns `{ data: { otp: \"...\", email: \"...\" } }`, an **API Verification Code Banner** appears with an **\"Auto-fill Code\"** button and 1-click copy action.\n   - Supports `/api/verify_otp` and `/api/resend_otp`.\n   - Upon successful registration and verification, redirects the user directly to the **Login page** (`/login?registered=true`) with a success banner.\n\n3. **Login Flow & Landing Page Navigation (`/login`)**\n   - Form fields: `email`, `password`, and `remember_me` sent to `/api/login`.\n   - On successful authentication, saves the Bearer token and user profile in context and `localStorage`, displays a success indicator, and immediately redirects the user to the **Landing page** (`/`).\n   - Landing page navigation bar dynamically updates to show the logged-in athlete\'s profile badge, member status, and a **Log Out** button that calls `/api/logout`.\n\n4. **Forgot & Reset Password Support (`/forgot-password`)**\n   - Integrates `/api/forgot-password` (returns OTP), `/api/forgot-verify-otp` (returns reset token), and `/api/reset-password` (sets new password with token) with OTP auto-fill from the API response.\n\n5. **Modular Component Architecture (Separate Files & Folders)**\n   - `src/lib/types/auth.ts`: TypeScript contracts for users and API responses.\n   - `src/lib/authApi.ts`: FormData client for all endpoints.\n   - `src/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts`: Server-side proxy ensuring CORS and network reliability.\n   - `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`: Session and authentication state provider.\n   - `src/components/auth/common/`: Reusable brand logos, input fields with password visibility toggle, backdrop droplets, and OTP banners.\n   - `src/components/auth/login/`: Dedicated `LoginForm` and `LoginCard`.\n   - `src/components/auth/register/`: Dedicated `RegisterForm` and `RegisterCard`.\n   - `src/components/auth/otp/`: Dedicated `OtpVerificationCard`.\n   - `src/components/auth/forgot-password/`: Dedicated `ForgotPasswordCard` and `ResetPasswordForm`.\n   - `src/app/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/register/page.tsx`, `src/app/verify-otp/page.tsx`, `src/app/forgot-password/page.tsx`: App Router pages."
    thinking: "**Assessing Current Progress**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the linting and compilation steps are successful for the applet. Now, I\'m focusing on the user\'s requirements. Specifically, I\'m reviewing the request to create Login and Registration pages that align with the landing page design. I\'m noting the color scheme, including the hex codes for the deep carbon colors.\n\n\n**Implementing User Redirects**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented the redirects for registration. The REGISTER button in the navigation now correctly points to the registration route, and both footer links work. After a successful registration, users are now prompted to verify their OTP, with the option to skip. Upon OTP verification or skip, they are then redirected to the login page, marked as registered. The successful login now redirects to the landing page.\n\n\n**Confirming Auth Flow**\n\nI\'m now certain the auth flow is functioning as intended, storing token and user data within `AuthContext` and `localStorage`. Upon successful login, the \"Login Successful!\" message briefly displays before navigating to the landing page. The landing page\'s `HeroTopNav` now correctly reflects the user\'s logged-in status with avatar, display name, role badge, and a logout button that calls `/api/logout`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Login and Registration pages matching the visual design of the Kratos Fitness landing page have been implemented, along with OTP verification, password recovery, and session management.\n\n### Key Additions & Features\n\n1. **Brand-Matched Design & Layout**\n   - **Visual Identity**: Implemented dark carbon palette (`#0E1012`, `#121417`), high-contrast lime green accents (`#71AC16`), Satoshi typography, organic droplet silhouettes, and athletic imagery matching the landing page.\n   - **Split Screen Presentation**: Desktop view displays an athlete hero showcase alongside the interactive form card; smoothly adapts to a focused card on mobile and tablet.\n\n2. **Registration Flow & OTP Integration (`/register`)**\n   - Form fields: `first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `password`, `password_confirmation`, and `terms` sent via `multipart/form-data` to `/api/register`.\n   - **OTP from API Response**: When the server returns `{ data: { otp: \"...\", email: \"...\" } }`, an **API Verification Code Banner** appears with an **\"Auto-fill Code\"** button and 1-click copy action.\n   - Supports `/api/verify_otp` and `/api/resend_otp`.\n   - Upon successful registration and verification, redirects the user directly to the **Login page** (`/login?registered=true`) with a success banner.\n\n3. **Login Flow & Landing Page Navigation (`/login`)**\n   - Form fields: `email`, `password`, and `remember_me` sent to `/api/login`.\n   - On successful authentication, saves the Bearer token and user profile in context and `localStorage`, displays a success indicator, and immediately redirects the user to the **Landing page** (`/`).\n   - Landing page navigation bar dynamically updates to show the logged-in athlete\'s profile badge, member status, and a **Log Out** button that calls `/api/logout`.\n\n4. **Forgot & Reset Password Support (`/forgot-password`)**\n   - Integrates `/api/forgot-password` (returns OTP), `/api/forgot-verify-otp` (returns reset token), and `/api/reset-password` (sets new password with token) with OTP auto-fill from the API response.\n\n5. **Modular Component Architecture (Separate Files & Folders)**\n   - `src/lib/types/auth.ts`: TypeScript contracts for users and API responses.\n   - `src/lib/authApi.ts`: FormData client for all endpoints.\n   - `src/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts`: Server-side proxy ensuring CORS and network reliability.\n   - `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`: Session and authentication state provider.\n   - `src/components/auth/common/`: Reusable brand logos, input fields with password visibility toggle, backdrop droplets, and OTP banners.\n   - `src/components/auth/login/`: Dedicated `LoginForm` and `LoginCard`.\n   - `src/components/auth/register/`: Dedicated `RegisterForm` and `RegisterCard`.\n   - `src/components/auth/otp/`: Dedicated `OtpVerificationCard`.\n   - `src/components/auth/forgot-password/`: Dedicated `ForgotPasswordCard` and `ResetPasswordForm`.\n   - `src/app/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/register/page.tsx`, `src/app/verify-otp/page.tsx`, `src/app/forgot-password/page.tsx`: App Router pages."
